WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.079 --> 00:00:05.270
Hey youtubers it's Charlie and today I wanted
to dedicate a video to Doctor Who Companions,

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:08.821
I already did some of my old favorites last
year so this time I wanted to talk about the

00:00:08.821 --> 00:00:11.590
top 10 people I want to see become new companions.

00:00:11.590 --> 00:00:14.290
We also have some more info on the actual
date of the Series 8 premiere so I'll start

00:00:14.290 --> 00:00:15.290
off with that.

00:00:15.290 --> 00:00:18.820
Because really the biggest thing we want to
know is when we get to start watching episodes

00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:19.820
again.

00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:21.460
If you're finding me for the first time I'm
going to be doing weekly Doctor Who bonus

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:22.970
videos up to the series 8 premiere.

00:00:22.970 --> 00:00:24.349
Be sure to subscribe to get everything.

00:00:24.349 --> 00:00:29.620
Once episodes start I'll be doing 3 videos
a week for episodes just like I do for game

00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:31.110
of thrones right now.

00:00:31.110 --> 00:00:33.980
I'll even be doing a weekly giveaway.

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:38.900
Important stuff first, there's a Doctor Who
World tour starting on August 7th in the UK

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:41.089
and ending August 19th in Brazil.

00:00:41.089 --> 00:00:44.981
The BBC announced Peter Capaldi and people
from the show will be promoting the series

00:00:44.981 --> 00:00:49.000
in a bunch of different cities in anticipation
of the series 8 premiere.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:52.590
That language is very important, in "Anticipation"
of the series 8 premiere.

00:00:52.590 --> 00:00:53.650
So what does that mean?

00:00:53.650 --> 00:00:58.260
Essentially Capaldi will be traveling around
doing press and then after the tour is over

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:00.120
they'll have the worldwide premiere.

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:06.220
August 19th is on a Tuesday, so tentatively
plan for the Series 8 premiere to be on Saturday

00:01:06.220 --> 00:01:08.030
August 23rd.

00:01:08.030 --> 00:01:11.040
It's totally possible they could have the
premiere in the middle of the tour or even

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:12.040
at the start of the tour.

00:01:12.040 --> 00:01:14.020
But because the BBC used the language "in
anticipation of", I think it implies they're

00:01:14.020 --> 00:01:17.000
trying to build excitement before the premiere,
not after it.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:20.721
I'll post a link in the description for all
the tour dates in case they're coming to your

00:01:20.721 --> 00:01:22.770
city and you want to try and go.

00:01:22.770 --> 00:01:23.770
They're visiting Seven cities total.

00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:24.770
Now let's talk about some new companions.

00:01:24.770 --> 00:01:28.350
The fun thing is that there can be a lot of
them, unless it's the 50th Anniversary or

00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:29.900
The Doctor is having vanity issues.

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:32.750
There can only be one of him in any given
episode.

00:01:32.750 --> 00:01:34.940
But companions can come and go all the time.

00:01:34.940 --> 00:01:37.030
So here are the top 10 new companions I'd
like to see in a future series.

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:38.860
They've almost finished series 8 filming,
so none of these people would make it this

00:01:38.860 --> 00:01:39.860
year.

00:01:39.860 --> 00:01:41.920
Number 10 - John Bradley from Game of Thrones

00:01:41.920 --> 00:01:43.950
Samwell on Doctor Who would be so much fun.

00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:48.140
There's a lot of historical figures he could
play like young Winston Churchill, but as

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:52.420
a companion I'd really like to see him play
a grown up version of Stormageddon.

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:55.850
He's already playing a good analog for Craig
on Game of Thrones.

00:01:55.850 --> 00:01:59.500
Plus he would get to be part of a meta sci
fi mashup with some other Game Of Thrones

00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:00.500
actors on my list.

00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:04.610
That's one of the things I love about british
series and series that film in Europe.

00:02:04.610 --> 00:02:05.880
You see a lot of the same actors bounce around.

00:02:05.880 --> 00:02:09.250
So a lot of people who have worked together
on Doctor Who have worked together on a lot

00:02:09.250 --> 00:02:11.230
of other series too.

00:02:11.230 --> 00:02:13.840
Number 9 - Antonia Thomas from Misfits

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:18.740
So she's acutally just been cast in Series
2 of The Musketeers which also stars Peter

00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:22.950
Capaldi, he's going to have to leave the show
because of Doctor Who commitments, but see

00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:25.950
what I mean about actors working together
on different series.

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:30.620
It's really her character on Misfits, if you
never saw it.

00:02:30.620 --> 00:02:34.580
A bunch of juvenile deliquents get caught
in a storm and get super powers.

00:02:34.580 --> 00:02:36.849
Hers was sexual attraction.

00:02:36.849 --> 00:02:41.510
She had River Song level pheromones, so she
would be an amazing as a companion on Doctor

00:02:41.510 --> 00:02:44.420
Who that may or may not be the daughter or
River Song.

00:02:44.420 --> 00:02:47.010
I know Jenny is supposed to be the Doctor's
Daughter, but it's just funny to think of

00:02:47.010 --> 00:02:51.099
the Doctor having an alternate universe version
of a daughter that takes after River more.

00:02:51.099 --> 00:02:55.560
Also fun fact, another Game of Thrones actor
who starred on Misfits with Antonia was Ewan

00:02:55.560 --> 00:02:58.750
Rheon who plays Ramsay Snow, now Ramsay Bolton.

00:02:58.750 --> 00:03:00.599
He'd make a good Doctor Who villain.

00:03:00.599 --> 00:03:02.200
Number 8 - Freya Mevor from Skins

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:06.810
On Skins she went from being like a mean girl
queen bee to a mother and a caregiver.

00:03:06.810 --> 00:03:10.381
You could say that all of the Doctor's female
companions end up taking care of him at some

00:03:10.381 --> 00:03:14.400
point so I'd really like to see her get something
of a modified Donna Noble arc where she goes

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:19.220
from meltdown celebutant to hero.

00:03:19.220 --> 00:03:24.850
Like remember between series 6 and series
7 when they did that weird plot with Amy becoming

00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:28.200
a super celebrity and her marriage with Rory
falling apart.

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:32.190
I wasn't a huge fan of that, but thematically
it fits.

00:03:32.190 --> 00:03:35.300
Freya as the celebrity getting swept up in
the Doctor's life.

00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:39.650
Fun Fact, Frey starred on Skins with two other
Game of Thrones actors Hannah Murray and Joe

00:03:39.650 --> 00:03:42.910
Dempsie who play Gilly and Gendry.

00:03:42.910 --> 00:03:45.200
Number 7 - Ruth Wilson from Luther

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:49.300
She's a little bit older than some of the
twenty something's Doctor Who usually casts

00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:54.490
as Companions, but I wanted to include a few
fantasy picks for actors who are just amazing.

00:03:54.490 --> 00:03:57.739
On Luther her Alice character is incredibly
sinister.

00:03:57.739 --> 00:04:01.700
Like River Song when she was still the insane
version of Melody Pond.

00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:03.739
She'd even make a fantastic Lady Time Lord.

00:04:03.739 --> 00:04:08.100
I think given the darker more serious tone
of Peter Capaldi's Doctor, she'd be a good

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:09.100
foil.

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:14.459
You don't always have to have silly companions,
so she's my choice for a devilish grin companion.

00:04:14.459 --> 00:04:17.329
Not an evil companion, just one that delights
in a little chaos.

00:04:17.329 --> 00:04:20.769
She's also one of the few actresses on my
list that looks amazing as a ginger and Paul

00:04:20.769 --> 00:04:23.849
McGann was a recurring guest star on Luther.

00:04:23.849 --> 00:04:25.629
Number 6 - Hannah Murray from Game of Thones

00:04:25.629 --> 00:04:29.939
I really just want to see Gilly become a Doctor
Who companion is what I'm saying.

00:04:29.939 --> 00:04:34.449
Like Samwell finds her a new place to hide
that just ends up being a police box conveniently

00:04:34.449 --> 00:04:36.860
parked in the library of Castle Black.

00:04:36.860 --> 00:04:39.550
She was also on Skins with Joe Dempsie.

00:04:39.550 --> 00:04:43.479
Her character Cassie Ainsworth was a total
mess of a human being with all kinds of problems

00:04:43.479 --> 00:04:44.479
with addiction and eating disorders.

00:04:44.479 --> 00:04:49.180
The Doctor is a healer, I'd really like to
see Hannah do a version of Cassie that becomes

00:04:49.180 --> 00:04:52.229
empowered as a result of her adventures in
the TARDIS.

00:04:52.229 --> 00:04:54.180
Not empowered like Bad Wolf empowered.

00:04:54.180 --> 00:05:02.839
But you get the idea.

00:05:02.839 --> 00:05:04.939
Number 5 - Laura Donnelly from Merlin

00:05:04.939 --> 00:05:08.080
On that show she played the character who
became the Lady of The Lake.

00:05:08.080 --> 00:05:12.110
She was a tragic character who was cursed
and fell in love with Merlin but eventually

00:05:12.110 --> 00:05:14.440
ascended to become this hugely important character.

00:05:14.440 --> 00:05:17.589
Very similar to Bad Wolf Rose Tyler.

00:05:17.589 --> 00:05:21.520
I don't want to see another romantic companion
so soon after River Song, but I do like the

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:22.830
idea of the ticking clock.

00:05:22.830 --> 00:05:25.629
They kind of did it with Clara and the Impossible
girl plot.

00:05:25.629 --> 00:05:30.699
But I'd like to see Laura play a companion
that the Doctor always knows will die soon.

00:05:30.699 --> 00:05:34.930
Like a reverse version of the Lake Silencio
plot in series 6, where the doctor always

00:05:34.930 --> 00:05:37.039
has to die at a fixed point.

00:05:37.039 --> 00:05:48.349
So using time travel they just avoid that
moment in time for a whole series.

00:05:48.349 --> 00:05:53.590
Fun Fact: Laura starred on Merlin with Eve
Myles of Torchwood, Joe Dempsie of Game of

00:05:53.590 --> 00:05:58.990
Thrones and John Hurt the 8.5 Doctor or 9th
Doctor, depending on how you look at it.

00:05:58.990 --> 00:06:00.939
Number 4 - Rose Leslie

00:06:00.939 --> 00:06:05.379
I don't want to post any Game of Thrones spoilers
about Ygritte here, but I'm such a fan of

00:06:05.379 --> 00:06:10.629
the previous ginger companion that I really
want Rose Leslie to be Ygritte to the Doctor's

00:06:10.629 --> 00:06:11.629
Jon Snow.

00:06:11.629 --> 00:06:15.439
Not in a romantic way, just a companion that
isn't going to take any of the Doctor's crap.

00:06:15.439 --> 00:06:19.330
All of my favorite companions were always
smarter and more helpful than the Doctor most

00:06:19.330 --> 00:06:20.409
of the time.

00:06:20.409 --> 00:06:22.210
Yes, the Doctor always comes through in the
end.

00:06:22.210 --> 00:06:26.069
But day to day, it's the Companion that usually
ends up seeming like the smart one.

00:06:26.069 --> 00:06:30.419
Rose Leslie would make an amazing young companion
who can order the Doctor around without seeming

00:06:30.419 --> 00:06:31.849
too bossy.

00:06:31.849 --> 00:06:33.930
Number 3 - Karla Chrome misfits

00:06:33.930 --> 00:06:38.960
On that show her superpower was seeing through
people's bullshit, like when they were lying.

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:43.539
I'd really like to see how that ability would
work when the first rule is "The Doctor Always

00:06:43.539 --> 00:06:44.539
Lies".

00:06:44.539 --> 00:06:47.509
Just imagine Capaldi saying random things
and her just going, "Bullshit" very softly

00:06:47.509 --> 00:06:48.509
in the background.

00:06:48.509 --> 00:06:51.819
Even just whispering it under her breath.

00:06:51.819 --> 00:06:53.749
Number 2 - Richard Ayoade

00:06:53.749 --> 00:06:57.599
He was actually rumored for the role of The
Doctor for a long time but I'm kind of glad

00:06:57.599 --> 00:07:01.460
they didn't pick him just because Matt Smith's
thing was being the sillier version of the

00:07:01.460 --> 00:07:04.099
Doctor and Ayoade is an excellent comedian.

00:07:04.099 --> 00:07:09.099
But a comedy driven Doctor for 6 or 8 years
in a row is just too much of the same.

00:07:09.099 --> 00:07:10.649
That's why I really want to see him as a companion.

00:07:10.649 --> 00:07:13.379
Just a really dry funny scientist or totally
unremarkable person who can punch up Capaldi's

00:07:13.379 --> 00:07:15.779
scenes if they get too dry.

00:07:15.779 --> 00:07:18.189
That's the thing I really love about British
humor.

00:07:18.189 --> 00:07:21.929
Sometimes it can be so subtle you don't realize
it's a joke.

00:07:21.929 --> 00:07:25.990
Most of the time I appreciate that kind of
humor more than the really obvious jokes you

00:07:25.990 --> 00:07:27.740
see in stuff like 22 Jump Street.

00:07:27.740 --> 00:07:30.659
There's at least one dick joke every five
minutes in that movie.

00:07:30.659 --> 00:07:31.669
And I laughed a lot.

00:07:31.669 --> 00:07:36.169
But I think Ayoade's dry humor would be so
much more appropriate for Doctor Who.

00:07:36.169 --> 00:07:40.899
Why else would they have considered him for
the Doctor if he wasn't perfect for the series?

00:07:40.899 --> 00:07:45.459
Number 1 - Kate McGrath from Merlin

00:07:45.459 --> 00:07:48.889
She plays Morgana on Merlin and I think she
would make an amazing companion.

00:07:48.889 --> 00:07:50.870
She would be my dream casting.

00:07:50.870 --> 00:07:53.689
Like a companion who could run circles around
the Doctor.

00:07:53.689 --> 00:08:02.139
I feel like the best companions should also
be people who would make amazing time lords.

00:08:02.139 --> 00:08:06.849
And in order to do that you have to be powerful
and really quick.

00:08:06.849 --> 00:08:09.119
Like Stephen Colbert quick, mentally that
is.

00:08:09.119 --> 00:08:10.680
Just like a machine gun of thoughts.

00:08:10.680 --> 00:08:16.180
I know a lot of you Game of Thrones fans would
like to see her play Lyanna Stark, but there's

00:08:16.180 --> 00:08:17.720
no reason she couldn't do both.

00:08:17.720 --> 00:08:20.370
There are like 3 Game of Thrones actors on
my list.

00:08:20.370 --> 00:08:23.780
One of the benefits of british series running
shorter than American series is that it leaves

00:08:23.780 --> 00:08:26.659
more time for the actors to do other shows.

00:08:26.659 --> 00:08:30.969
So Morgana Pendragon gets my number 1 vote
for a future companion.

00:08:30.969 --> 00:08:35.860
Now it's your turn though, which actor or
actress would you like to see as a companion?

00:08:35.860 --> 00:08:38.870
Bonus points for crossing the fandom streams.

00:08:38.870 --> 00:08:41.960
Since I'm posting this kind of late I'm not
going to have time to do an Orphan Black video

00:08:41.960 --> 00:08:42.960
tonight.

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:45.590
So I'll just be doing some tumblr gifs and
writing my thoughts down there.

00:08:45.590 --> 00:08:49.040
You're also welcome to ask me questions about
that in these comments.

00:08:49.040 --> 00:08:52.930
My next Doctor Who video will post next Saturday,
I haven't quite decided what it's going to

00:08:52.930 --> 00:08:55.210
be but feel free to leave me suggestions.

00:08:55.210 --> 00:08:59.960
Right now click here to get ready for the
big Game of Thrones finale this weekend and

00:08:59.960 --> 00:09:02.410
click here to learn more about the series
8 episodes.

00:09:02.410 --> 00:09:04.240
Thanks for watching, see you guys tomorrow.

00:09:04.240 --> 00:09:04.610
High Fives!

